<%# locals: (workspace:) %>
<%# CONTENT ONLY — the caller owns the <li> and its chrome.
    This renders in three containers: the pinned current row's plain <ul>, the
    other-workspaces <ul>, and the archived UI::ListGroup. No single padding is
    right in all three, and hard-coding one here is what put three paddings
    inside identical list chrome, two of them in the same <ul> (#1119).
    The comment this replaces said the partial rendered only inside the
    archived ListGroup. That stopped being true at cd6f0263. %>
<p class="font-medium text-text-heading"><%= t("workspaces.locked_row.heading") %></p>
<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-body"><%= t("workspaces.locked_row.body", name: workspace.name) %></p>
<%= link_to t("workspaces.locked_row.contact"), contact_path,
      class: "mt-3 inline-flex btn-touch-target btn-text btn-text-interactive text-sm" %>
